@startuml provider_identity_model
title Provider Identity and Runtime Contract

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/models.ts: Provider (lines 88-149), MutableModels (lines 225-230), createProvider (lines 739-862)
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/types.ts: ProviderId (lines 35-76), Model (lines 820-850)
' Observed behavior: provider.id is the registry key and Model.provider selects the owning provider.
' Design reason: identity, protocol dispatch, model identity, and mutable connection data must remain separate.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
  ArrowColor #475569
}

class ProviderIdentity {
  +providerId: string
}

class ProviderRuntimeContract {
  +displayName: string
  +baseUrl: optional string
  +headers: optional map
  +auth: required
  +getModels(): Model[]
  +refreshModels(): optional
  +filterModels(): optional
  +stream(model, context, options)
  +cancelActiveResponse(responseId): optional
}

class ModelIdentity {
  +providerId: string
  +modelId: string
}

class ModelDescriptor {
  +modelId: string
  +apiId: string
  +capabilities
  +limits
  +cost
}

class ApiProtocol {
  +apiId: string
  +stream implementation
}

ProviderIdentity "1" *-- "1" ProviderRuntimeContract : identifies
ProviderIdentity "1" *-- "0..*" ModelIdentity : owns
ModelIdentity "1" *-- "1" ModelDescriptor : describes
ModelDescriptor --> ApiProtocol : dispatches by apiId
ProviderRuntimeContract --> ApiProtocol : supplies one or more

note right of ProviderIdentity
Only providerId determines identity.
Name, URL, credentials, and apiId
may change without changing identity.
end note

note bottom of ModelIdentity
Runtime model key is
(providerId, modelId).
end note
@enduml

@startuml generic_provider_boundary
title Generic Model Manager Provider Boundary

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/models.ts: ModelsImpl.requireProvider and stream (lines 628-695)
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/api/openai-responses.ts: buildParams and stream (lines 99-189 and 273-344)
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/CampusClawAiService.java: resolveProvider (lines 141-147)
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAIResponsesProvider.java: buildParams and handleResponseEvent
' mate-service README.md: model gateway gap (line 116)
' Architecture change: Java resolves an AiProvider by model.providerId instead of resolving an ApiProvider by model.api.
' Security hardening: upstream endpoints, credentials, provider ids, and vendor model ids remain inside mate-service.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

package "pi-mono-java Runtime" {
  [AgentLoop] as Loop
  [CampusClawAiService] as AiService
  [AiProviderRegistry] as Registry
  [MateServiceModelManagerProvider\nproviderId = mate-model-manager\napiId = openai-responses] as GenericProvider
  [ManagedModelCatalogClient] as CatalogClient
  [ManagedModelInvocationClient] as InvocationClient
}

package "mate-service" {
  [Internal Model Manager API] as ManagerApi
  [Model Authorization] as Authorization
  [OpenAI Responses Router] as Router
  database "t_model_provider\nt_model_definition\nt_agent_binding_models" as Catalog
  [Secret Store] as Secrets
  [OpenAI Responses Proxy] as Adapters
}

cloud "Upstream LLM Services" as Vendors

Loop --> AiService : model + Context + options
AiService --> Registry : get(model.providerId)
Registry --> GenericProvider
GenericProvider --> CatalogClient
GenericProvider --> InvocationClient
CatalogClient --> ManagerApi : HTTPS JSON
InvocationClient --> ManagerApi : Responses JSON and SSE
ManagerApi --> Authorization : catalog operations 2 and 3 only
Authorization --> Catalog
ManagerApi --> Router : exact Mate modelId
Router --> Catalog
Router --> Secrets : credentialRef
Router --> Adapters
Adapters --> Vendors

note bottom of GenericProvider
The Runtime sees one provider and opaque modelIds.
It never receives upstream credentials or endpoints.
end note
@enduml

@startuml model_manager_invocation_sequence
title Mate OpenAI Responses Invocation and Cancellation

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/api/openai-responses.ts: stream and buildParams (lines 99-189 and 273-344)
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/api/openai-responses-shared.ts: convertResponsesMessages and processResponsesStream (lines 131-342 and 500-792)
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAIResponsesProvider.java: buildParams, handleResponseEvent, and convertInputItems
' pi-mono-java modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java: invokeModel and consumeStream (lines 198-288)
' OpenAI API: POST /responses and POST /responses/{response_id}/cancel
' Target-only design: mate-service Responses create and foreground cancel operations do not exist yet.
' Product authorization: invocation authenticates the service caller and does not receive or validate agentId.
' OpenAI compatibility extension: Mate cancels active foreground streams although official cancel requires background=true.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor Client
participant "AgentLoop" as Loop
participant "CampusClawAiService" as AiService
participant "AiProviderRegistry" as Registry
participant "MateServiceModelManagerProvider" as Provider
participant "mate-service Responses Proxy" as Manager
participant "OpenAI Responses Endpoint" as OpenAI

Client -> Loop : submit prompt
Loop -> AiService : stream(model, Context, options)
AiService -> Registry : get(model.providerId)
Registry --> AiService : generic Provider
AiService -> Provider : streamSimple(model, Context, options)
Provider -> Provider : convert Context to Responses input array
Provider -> Manager : POST /responses\nmodel + input + tools + safe options
Manager -> Manager : authenticate service caller
Manager -> Manager : validate request allowlist\nand resolve exact Mate modelId
Manager -> Manager : replace model with upstreamModelId\nand inject endpoint and credential
Manager -> OpenAI : POST /responses\nstream=true and store=false

loop OpenAI Responses SSE
  OpenAI --> Manager : Responses event
  Manager -> Manager : preserve response.id\nand rewrite response.model
  Manager --> Provider : Responses event
  Provider -> Provider : store responseId and map event
  Provider --> Loop : AssistantMessageEvent
end

alt Abort after response.created
  Loop -> Provider : cancel subscription
  Provider -> Manager : POST /responses/{responseId}/cancel
  Manager -> OpenAI : abort active foreground stream
  Manager --> Provider : 200 Response with status cancelled
  Manager --> Provider : close original SSE
  Provider --> Loop : StopReason.ABORTED
else Abort before response.created
  Loop -> Provider : cancel subscription
  Provider -> Manager : close create stream
  Provider --> Loop : StopReason.ABORTED
else Response already terminal
  Provider -> Manager : POST /responses/{responseId}/cancel
  Manager --> Provider : 404 RESPONSE_NOT_ACTIVE
end

note over Provider,Manager
No automatic create POST replay after an unknown outcome.
Cancellation emits no synthetic Responses terminal event.
Tool execution stays in AgentLoop.
end note
@enduml

@startuml java_provider_alignment
title Java Provider Alignment with pi-mono

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/models.ts: Provider and Models registry keyed by provider.id
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/api/openai-responses-shared.ts: Context conversion and Responses stream processing
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/ApiProviderRegistry.java: registry keyed by Api (lines 22-152)
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAIResponsesProvider.java: partial Responses mapper
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/types/Provider.java: closed enum with CUSTOM (lines 19-37)
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/config/CustomModelLoader.java: every custom model uses Provider.CUSTOM (lines 92-123)
' Java divergence: the current Java design models protocol adapters as providers and cannot preserve arbitrary provider identity.
' Architecture change: add open ProviderId and ApiId values, resolve AiProvider by providerId, and keep protocol routing internal.

